  "result": "A refused approval must change nothing. Every invoice field keeps its value, and the repository's `Update` is not called. The refusal does not count as a rejection, so the invoice never gets `Rejected`. The refusal reason must name the rule, role, limit and invoice. The API returns 403 with `{ error, code }`, and the web UI shows the server's `error` text.\n\nRules are checked first and the write happens only after they all pass, because the repository hands out live objects and a field written before a refusal would leave the store changed even without `Update`.\n\nSource: `AGENTS.md`, \"Approval rules\" (FR-005), \"Layering\", and \"Never\" sections.",
